00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.350 align:start position:0%
phonemen diagrams are very useful  because they take the complicated and  abstract mathematics of particle  interactions  and show the equations as simple  pictures of what happens when subatomic  particles interact  the axes of feynman diagrams are space  and time and the different particles get  different lines  a photon is a wiggle the gluons are  spirals the w  and z bosons and the higgs boson get a  dotted line and the fermions get  straight lines with arrows  these arrows point forwards in time for  mata particles and backwards in time for  antimatter  particles and the arrows always flow  from one side of the diagram to the  other  the building blocks of feynman diagrams  are vertices which are a joining point  between  three particles the orientation of these  vertices changes the story they're  telling  this one shows an electron changing  momentum when it emits a photon  but if you rotate it it shows an  electron and positron annihilation into  a photon  you can build most fundament diagrams  from this set of vertices  like this or this if you want more  information check out my full video in  the description
 

